From fc7db189c640631860fed92ecd1f7840ec762c81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolzen <funer@gmx.at>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:28:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] init: Manage system services with runit when booted with it

Fan control, firmware debug and the CPU scheduler controlled their
services through org.freedesktop.systemd1 only. On runit systems such
as Void Linux, foo.service now maps to the runit service foo, so the
existing configuration works unchanged. systemd stays in use wherever
it is booted or no init system is detected.
